# RBWS FVI Extractor

Recreate gold-layout RBWS Excel from Jimcel FVI Fire Water PDFs. Local only: native text or Tesseract, then rules. Do not call LLMs.

## Flow

PDF → render PNG → native text or OCR → `jimcel_native` or `ocr/parsers` → crop photos → `excel/writer`.

CLI: `src/rbws_extractor/main.py` via `OcrPipeline`.

## Rows

- Master list = Visual Inspection Observation tables.
- NOT APPLICABLE → zero rows.
- One item = one row (do not row-per-photo).
- Piping: Line # = tagged WF-…; full From–To; skip good-condition.
- Cylinders: Line # = `Fire protection cylinder`; Line Description = Equipment ID / location.
- Hose/monitor: Line # = Equipment Tag as written (`No tag found` stays).
- Pump/caisson: Line # = `Fire water pump & caisson`; one aggregated row, or none if N/A.
- Anomaly = table text + one photo range, not caption dumps.
- Judgment columns always blank (pressure, POF, risk, recommendations, remarks).

## Fill vs blank

Fill: S/N, Insp Date, Line #, Line Description, Anomaly Description, P&ID No, Photos.

P&ID: table/row value, not cover list. Blank for cylinders/pump only if that is the gold rule for that report family.

## Key files

`pipeline/ocr_pipeline.py`, `ocr/engine.py`, `ocr/jimcel_native.py`, `ocr/parsers.py`, `ocr/crop.py`, `excel/writer.py`, `configs/rbws_columns.yaml`
